\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0  And can it be that I should gain
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj An interest in the Saviour's blood?
\par Died He for me, who caused His pain?
\par For me, who Him to death pursue?
\par Amazing love! How can it be
\par That Thou, my God, shouldst die for me!
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. 'Tis mystery all! The Immortal dies:
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Who can explore His strange design?
\par In vain the first-born seraph tries
\par To sound the depths of love divine.
\par 'Tis mercy all! Let earth adore,
\par Let angel minds inquire no more.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. He left His Father's throne above
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 So free, so infinite His grace
\par Emptied Himself of all but love,
\par And bled for Adam's helpless race.
\par 'Tis mercy all, immense and free;
\par For, O my God, it found out me!
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 
\par \pard\fi-225\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.  Long my imprisoned spirit lay
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0\qj  Fast bound in sin and nature's night;
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj  Thine eye diffused a quickening ray
\par  I woke, the dungeon flamed with light;
\par  My chains fell off, my heart was free,
\par  I rose, went forth, and followed Thee.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  5.   No condemnation now I dread;
\par \pard\li144\sl190\slmult0    Jesus, and all in Him, is mine!
\par    Alive in Him, my living Head,
\par    And clothed in righteousness divine,
\par    Bold I approach the eternal throne,
\par \pard\li144\sl190\slmult0\qj    And claim the crown, through Christ, my own.\f1 
\par \pard\cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

